p('The AMP module used AMPir, AMPlify and Macrel. ARG detection used ABRicate, AMRFinderPlus, DeepARG, fARGene and RGI. Outputs were standardized using hAMRonization, and selected ABRicate, AMRFinderPlus and DeepARG outputs were mapped to ARO terms using argNorm.',[344,345])
p('BGC detection used antiSMASH, DeepBGC and GECCO. BiG-SLiCE outputs were not incorporated into the study’s BGC-family definitions. CAZyme annotation used run_dbCAN; the source describes HMMER, DIAMOND and Hotpep detection streams.',[346,347])
p('Functional outputs were reconciled to Prokka v1.15.6 annotations. Completion was assessed using expected module-specific output artifacts, with primary outputs retained and subsequent integration performed on derived files.',[348,349,350])
check('Software version/parameter required for Nextflow, profile/container, active gene caller, each module and database release. Verify the executed run_dbCAN evidence streams and retained outputs from logs; workflow capability is not proof that an option was run. Sequence-format checks alone do not exclude fragmentation effects.')
h('13. Functional-feature harmonization, clustering and Panaroo mapping')
p('AMP sequences and coordinate-supported Tier-A AMR proteins were grouped at 50% amino-acid identity and 80% bidirectional coverage. AMP confidence was assessed using predictor concordance and exported curated AMP evidence. AMR records underwent conservative family normalization and evidence-stream consolidation. Overlapping BGC predictions were consolidated at ≥50% overlap of the shorter region. Because BiG-SCAPE analysis was unavailable, BGC families were defined by exact normalized product type and PFAM-domain composition. CAZyme summaries used primary-consensus calls.',[77,79,80,81,84,89,91,94,96])
p('FuncScan-derived features were mapped to existing Panaroo clusters. Frequency-class comparisons used unique mapped clusters, not occurrence-weighted counts. Genome-by-family multicopy summaries were generated for Panaroo groups and AMR homolog groups; gene-tree reconstruction was not performed.',[108,109,112])
check('Software version/parameter required: clustering algorithm/representative selection, Tier-A definition, AMR normalization dictionary, locus deduplication rules, AMP confidence rule and match thresholds, coordinate extraction, BGC overlap transitivity and multi-label handling, domain normalization, CAZyme consensus rule, mapping overlap/identity criteria and unmapped-feature accounting. Supply enrichment tests, background denominators and multicopy definitions.')
h('14. Cross-functional associations, burden modelling, proximity and networks')
p('Genome-level feature presence/absence comparisons excluded invariant and extremely rare features and evaluated AMP–AMR, AMP–BGC and ARG–BGC pairs. Benjamini–Hochberg-adjusted q-values and Phi coefficients summarized associations; q<0.05 defined significance, with |Phi|≥0.20 used to identify stronger effects. Coordinate-mappable co-occurrences were evaluated for same-contig separation and proximity within 10 kb. The functional network retained q<0.05 and |Phi|≥0.50 and used Louvain communities.',[99,100,101,102,115])
p('Functional burden associations were summarized using Spearman correlations, bootstrap intervals, CDS-adjusted partial correlations and count regression reporting incidence-rate ratios. The manuscript reports no phylogenetic correction for the functional network.',[104,105,106,115])
check('Software version/parameter required: rarity cutoff, statistical test/sidedness, odds-ratio zero-cell handling, BH testing families, bootstrap repetitions/seed, partial-correlation algorithm, regression family/link/formula/diagnostics and scaling, distance definition for overlapping or multiple loci and circular contigs, and Louvain weighting/sign handling/resolution/seed. Include the within-AMR qacEdelta1–sul1 association procedure. This section documents associations, not resistance-prediction machine learning.')
